{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","max_tokens":64000,"stream":true,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"summarized","block_binding":{"prefix_mismatch_behavior":"drop_block"}},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"},"cache_control":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"},"fallbacks":"default","tools":[{"description":"Attach a file from the user's computer to this tool's result so you can inspect it in your next step: a screenshot you took, a chart or page a script drew, a document, a log or a source file. Text comes back as text: up to 2,000 lines and 50 KiB, or else only the start of the file. Any other file is attached whole, as it is, with its media type, and the provider decides whether it can read it. If it can't, or the file is too large, the result says so, and that file can't be read in this session. Images over 2,000 px on their long edge can't be attached. You may pass at most one of `pages`, `seconds` or `sheet` to ask a supporting model to read only that part of a document, audio/video file or spreadsheet. Models that don't support slices refuse locally without sending the file; when a sliced read is accepted, the whole file is still uploaded, stored and resent in the conversation until compaction. Attached files stay in the conversation, so view only the files you need. A relative path is resolved against the working directory, and ~ is the user's home.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"pages":{"description":"Read only this 1-based page or closed page range of a PDF, document or slide deck, such as \"5\" or \"14-16\". The whole file is still sent and stored.","type":"string"},"path":{"description":"The file to look at.","type":"string"},"seconds":{"description":"Read only this closed whole-second range of an audio or video file, such as \"0-30\" or \"120-210\" (end greater than start). The whole file is still sent and stored.","type":"string"},"sheet":{"description":"Read only this 1-based worksheet number of a spreadsheet, such as 2. The whole file is still sent and stored.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"},"name":"view_file"}],"system":[{"type":"text","text":"You are Wisp, a helpful assistant running in a terminal. Answer clearly and concisely; use plain text and Markdown sparingly. You can attach a file on the user's computer to your context with the view_file tool. A user message may begin with a 'Sent:' line that Wisp adds, giving the time it was sent; use it for anything involving dates or time, and don't mention it otherwise. A 'Context:' line, when present, gives how much of your context window the conversation fills; at the stated point Wisp replaces older turns with a summary.","cache_control":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<environment>\nWorking directory: <masked>\nPlatform: <masked>\nResources: <masked>\n</environment>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Terminal: replies are 156 columns wide (wider code blocks wrap), 30 rows; don't mention this.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Sent: <masked> UTC+05:30\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Context: <masked> of 1M tokens (0%). Wisp compacts at 850k.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"hello"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"GOLDEN-DONE"}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sent: <masked> UTC+05:30\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Context: <masked> of 1M tokens (0%). Wisp compacts at 850k.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"again"}]},{"role":"system","content":[{"type":"tool_addition","tool":{"type":"tool_definition","definition":{"description":"Show the user a diff in the chat. Use it when you want the user to see a change: one you propose, one you made, or a comparison they asked for. It only displays the diff: it changes no files and runs nothing, so it never applies a change. The user sees the diff with changed words and syntax highlighted, so don't repeat it in your reply.\n\nGive each file as `before` and `after` (the old and new text; Wisp computes the diff and shows 3 unchanged lines around each change) or as `diff` (a unified diff you wrote; wrong hunk line counts are recounted, and hunk headers without line numbers are accepted). Give `path` so the code gets syntax colours, or `language` when there is no path. Limits: 20 files, 10,000 lines and 512 KiB for each side of a file, 1 MiB in all.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"files":{"description":"The files to show, in order, one entry per file.","items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"after":{"description":"The new text. Use \"\" for a deleted file.","type":"string"},"before":{"description":"The old text. Use \"\" for a new file.","type":"string"},"diff":{"description":"A unified diff of this file, instead of before and after.","type":"string"},"language":{"description":"The language for syntax colours when path doesn't show it, such as rust.","type":"string"},"path":{"description":"The file's path, shown to the user.","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"maxItems":20,"minItems":1,"type":"array"},"title":{"description":"A short heading for the diff, such as what the change does.","type":"string"}},"required":["files"],"type":"object"},"name":"show_diff"}}},{"type":"text","text":"You can show the user a change as a diff with the show_diff tool."}]}]}
